  "body": "The JS spec uses ? when calling an abstract algorithm which might throw, and ! when calling an abstract algorithm and asserting that it won't throw. It seems like a lot of web specs are based around exceptions implicitly being propagated (as in JS), but other times, e.g., in some places in HTML, I see ? and ! explicitly as in JS. It would be good to clarify what is the best practice in this document. For example, should we use ? or ! whenever \"calling into\" JS, and never otherwise?",
